course: dictionary
lesson: 4449
title: Hangnails and healthy hands
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hangnail is a small torn piece of skin hanging loose beside or under a fingernail. It can hurt, but it is only skin, not a part of the nail itself.
explain: You can work out the meaning from the context. «A hangnail is clipped with clean clippers, because pulling it tears the skin and can cause infection.» Clipping, clippers and torn skin are clues that it is a bit of skin. Try the meaning in the sentence: "a small torn piece of skin is clipped with clean clippers". It still makes sense.
explain: The word is built from two smaller words, hang and nail, which tells you where it is: it hangs off the nail. Do not bite or pull it. Snip it carefully with clean clippers, wash your hands and keep the skin moisturised.
fact: A hangnail is a small torn piece of skin at the side or bottom of a fingernail.
fact: «Hangnail» is a noun. You can have one hangnail or two hangnails.
fact: Hangnails often come from dry skin and from biting your nails.
fact: Pulling a hangnail can tear the skin further, and germs can get in and cause infection.
fact: To look after a hangnail, snip it carefully with clean clippers, wash your hands and keep the skin moisturised.
exercise: «A hangnail is clipped with clean clippers, because pulling it tears the skin and can cause infection.» What is a hangnail? | A type of finger bone | A germ that lives under nails | A long nail that grows too fast | *A small torn piece of skin beside a fingernail
exercise: The sentence suggests what you should do with a hangnail. What is it? | Leave it alone so it tears more | Bite it off with your teeth | Pull it hard until it comes off | *Snip it carefully with clean clippers
exercise: What is a common cause of hangnails? | Eating too many apples | *Dry skin and nail biting | Wearing gloves | Running fast
test: Why should you not pull a hangnail? | Pulling is against the rules of the playground | *Pulling tears the skin and can cause infection | Pulling makes your hands warmer | Pulling makes your nail grow faster
test: After snipping a hangnail, what should you do? | Dip your finger in ink | Bite the rest of it off | *Wash your hands and keep the skin moisturised | Go to sleep with it still hanging
exam: Which is the best way to look after a hangnail? | Bite it and pull it hard | Ignore it until it falls off by itself | Cover it with glue | *Snip it with clean clippers, then wash your hands
